    <string name="text_ayuda">Welcome to the MINESWEEPER game!</string>
    <string name="text_ayuda1">The game consists of clearing all the squares on a grid that do not hide a mine. Some squares contain a number.</string>
    <string name="text_ayuda2">This number indicates how many mines are in the surrounding squares. So, if a square shows the number 3, it means that out of the eight surrounding squares (if it is not on an edge or corner), 3 contain mines and 5 do not.</string>
    <string name="text_ayuda4">If you uncover a square with a mine, YOU LOSE the game.</string>
    <string name="text_ayuda5">Otherwise, if you uncover all non-mine squares, YOU WIN!!</string>
    <string name="text_ayuda6">You can configure the number of rows in the grid, the percentage of mines, and whether to set a time limit to complete the game.</string>
